/-!
# The ellipsoid with a given shape matrix

The papers' `E(Q, q) = {x | (x − q)ᵀ Q⁻¹ (x − q) ≤ 1}` ([1, Eq. 5], [2, Sec. 1.1 (ellipse)]) takes
the shape matrix `Q` directly. The tree stores a generator `G` with `Q = G Gᵀ`, so the ellipsoid
of a given positive semi-definite `Q` is generated by its symmetric square root, `G = Q^(1/2)`,
whose product with its transpose is `Q` (`shape_ofShape`) and whose points are those of the
quadratic form (`mem_ofShape_iff`).

## References

* [1] A. Halder. "On the parameterized computation of minimum volume outer ellipsoid of
      Minkowski sum of ellipsoids". In Proc. of the 57th IEEE Conference on Decision and
      Control (CDC), pp. 4040-4045, 2018. arXiv:1803.08157.
* [2] M. Černý. "Goffin's algorithm for zonotopes". Kybernetika, 48(5):890-906, 2012.
-/

